dministration, custody, transfer agency, audit, legal, board, insurance, and exchange and data fees. Sponsor overhead and platform distribution payments are typically sponsor-borne.\n\n**Seed assets vs. expenditure:** Seed capital is a sponsor-owned investment, not an expense. It stays on the balance sheet and is recovered as shares are sold and redeemed. Only the costs above are expenditure.\n\n**Break-even:** Let F be annual fixed costs, f the fee rate, and v variable cost as a share of AUM. Break-even AUM is F / (f − v). Retained margin is positive only above that level. Treat the seed's cost of capital as an opportunity-cost hurdle, not a cash expense.","ttft_ms":5225,"type":"result","duration_ms":6613,"uuid":"775bfb17-9789-401a-8209-4743627ff7a5","ttft_stream_ms":392,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":392,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
